Here in Brazil we make stewed beans, and usually eat them with rice.
Actually beans and rice ("feijão com arroz") are the most common meal
in Brazil. In the northeast (where I'm from) is also common to add
cassava flour ("farinha de mandioca").
http://www.recipehound.com/Recipes/3929.html

Another famous dish with stewed beans here is called "feijoada";
basically stewed black beans with cured beef, sausage and/or pork
pieces. http://www.recipezaar.com/recipe/getrecipe.zsp?id=13938
